    "created_at": "2024-05-06T02:56:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-05-06T02:56:42Z",
    "body": "In general, the various hooks that DOM provides (largely for HTML's consumption by my estimation) like [attribute change steps](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-attributes-change-ext), [insertion steps](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-insert-ext) etc., seem to be [underspecified ordering-wise](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#ref-for-concept-element-attributes-change-ext%E2%91%A1). DOM provides a per-specification hook, which doesn't specify ordering across specs, and also HTML seems to provide _multiple_ overrides for some of these hooks, as you've found, which is bad form.\r\n\r\nProbably most of the time this is fine since I would guess(??) the steps are often mutually-non-observable, but I imagine this system has grown into a larger mess than it was originally conceived to be, so an issue filed against DOM to track cleaning that up is probably best (unless Anne has more historical context that I don't know about).\r\n\r\nFor this specific instance about popover, I would delegate to @josepharhar who has more domain-specific context than I. But also happy to take a look myself if needed.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
